  "internal_thinking": "Bob is offering 1 Wood for 1 Wheat. Looking at my resources, I have 2 Wood and 2 Wheat (after the recent roll of 9). My current goal is to reach 5 VP. I have 3 VP visible and a hidden Knight card. If I play that Knight on my next turn, I will have 3 Knights (1 revealed, 1 hidden, plus the one I just mentioned), giving me Largest Army for +2 VP, totaling 5 VP and the win. To play the Knight, I don't need Wood or Wheat (I already have them). However, I need to protect my lead. Bob is trying to build towards the Wheat Port and needs Wood for roads. Giving him Wheat might help him, but I already have plenty of Wood (2) and my Wood production (Nodes 14 and 7) is decent. I don't actually need more Wood right now. Wheat is more valuable for potential city upgrades or buying another development card if my win condition is blocked. Since I'm one turn away from potentially winning with Largest Army, I should avoid helping Bob accelerate his expansion. I will reject the trade.",
  "action": {
    "type": "trade_reject",
    "parameters": "{}"
  },
  "note_to_self": "I have 2 Wood, 2 Wheat, 1 Sheep, and a hidden Knight. Playing the Knight on my next turn will give me Largest Army and the win (5 VP). Rejected Bob's wood-for-wheat trade to keep my resources for potential pivots and prevent him from reaching the Wheat Port faster.",
